WEBVTT

00:00:04.487 --> 00:00:14.397
The basis of collectivity, the foundation
of collectivity, is very deep.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:22.671
And the deep understanding can only tell you

00:00:23.637 --> 00:00:32.701
that the basis of collectivity
is detached love.

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:34.383
Love is the only way.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:46.880
It's not possible to have collectivity
unless and until you have detached love.

00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:54.431
French have been good at so many types of
love that they have been talking about.

00:00:56.083 --> 00:01:00.921
And they have written books after books,
novels after novels, and have created

00:01:00.987 --> 00:01:12.163
lots of romantic and unromantic and
all kinds of atmospheres to talk of love.

00:01:13.071 --> 00:01:21.080
But the pure love,
as we understand in Sahaja Yoga,

00:01:21.168 --> 00:01:26.983
is to be now expressed by Sahaja Yogis among themselves.

00:01:33.948 --> 00:01:39.757
After all, we are all human beings
made by one God.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:50.328
And that we are all Sahaja Yogis
created by one mother.

00:01:52.332 --> 00:01:59.776
So, there should be no misunderstanding
between us of any kind.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:10.103
But we must know what sometimes
makes us little different.

00:02:11.486 --> 00:02:18.284
If we can understand the problems that we
face, then it would be much easier

00:02:18.365 --> 00:02:27.159
for us to see why our love becomes so attached
and not so detached.

00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:34.454
Starts becoming smaller and smaller.

00:02:35.981 --> 00:02:41.242
Then a person just starts loving oneself only.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:52.061
One of the main reasons that we have this
problem is because of our conditionings.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:03:02.764
We are conditioned the way that
we don't know how to love.

00:03:04.898 --> 00:03:09.035
When I see the advertisements
in the West.

00:03:09.115 --> 00:03:12.452
I don't know from where the
West starts and

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:15.914
where it ends, and
from where the East ends.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:20.693
They talk of West and East, but I don't
know which is the demarcating line.

00:03:20.774 --> 00:03:23.642
Can anybody tell me that?

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.253
Where do we start, East and West?

00:03:27.334 --> 00:03:31.798
Because it's one round world, you see.

00:03:34.427 --> 00:03:41.111
But somehow or other there is some line,
unknown line, underlying line,

00:03:41.191 --> 00:03:49.617
which creates sometimes this East and West, two types of conditionings.

00:03:53.033 --> 00:04:00.187
So when I see some advertisements,
they show about —

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.113
recently I saw about James Bond,

00:04:04.193 --> 00:04:15.207
that he is free to kill and the best film for revenge.

00:04:17.077 --> 00:04:19.667
This is the advertisement.

00:04:22.255 --> 00:04:31.025
If revenge is the best way of fulfillment,
then how can we love someone?

00:04:35.368 --> 00:04:41.022
So this kind of conditioning comes to us from outside,

00:04:41.477 --> 00:04:46.344
that we should not forgive anyone.

00:04:47.013 --> 00:04:49.735
We should take the revenge.

00:04:49.816 --> 00:04:57.788
And, if you do not take the revenge,
then you are not worthy your name.

00:04:58.457 --> 00:05:01.841
So if you cannot take the revenge

00:05:01.922 --> 00:05:08.189
like a duel that they used to have in France
quite a lot between the two persons.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:11.653
They would take two guns and kill each other.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:16.528
I mean what a stupid idea it was. Just think of it in modern times.

00:05:16.769 --> 00:05:18.501
But it was so.

00:05:19.845 --> 00:05:24.106
So if the revenge is not
taken,

00:05:24.522 --> 00:05:33.712
then it was thought to be something very sly, very low level.

00:05:34.059 --> 00:05:37.596
So a person must take revenge.

00:05:38.465 --> 00:05:44.345
History shows also the same things, that

00:05:44.425 --> 00:05:51.746
one had to take a revenge of

00:05:51.827 --> 00:05:58.315
another person who has harmed you; in any way troubled you.

00:05:58.396 --> 00:06:05.091
I think it's the quality of a snake, they
say, that if you step onto any snake,

00:06:05.304 --> 00:06:10.708
it follows you all his life
to take the revenge.

00:06:11.631 --> 00:06:14.534
The only thing that it does
all its life is

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:20.104
to run after that person who has, by mistake,

00:06:20.185 --> 00:06:23.151
put the foot on its body.

00:06:24.344 --> 00:06:30.405
In the same way, a human endeavour I have seen in so many novels is suggested

00:06:30.486 --> 00:06:37.639
how a man gets after a person who has some way or other harmed.

00:06:39.392 --> 00:06:44.012
If we go on like this,
there's no end to it.

00:06:44.531 --> 00:06:50.656
Firstly, it is absolutely absurd.

00:06:52.935 --> 00:06:56.496
For that I will give you
an example of Buddha.

00:06:56.576 --> 00:07:02.356
Very much I have been impressed by the way he said once.

00:07:02.436 --> 00:07:09.675
Somebody who insulted him and abused him and said all kinds of horrible words.

00:07:10.136 --> 00:07:12.941
Then Buddha went to another village.

00:07:13.022 --> 00:07:16.118
Now this fellow felt the remorse
and he went back,

00:07:16.199 --> 00:07:23.454
went back and said, "Sir, I'm sorry, I've said these things to you.

00:07:23.535 --> 00:07:26.024
I'm really very sorry."

00:07:26.338 --> 00:07:28.417
He said, "What?"

00:07:28.575 --> 00:07:31.480
"Well," he said, "Yesterday —."

00:07:31.564 --> 00:07:34.833
He said, "Yesterday is finished now.

00:07:35.007 --> 00:07:38.036
You are now with me today.

00:07:38.117 --> 00:07:42.074
So why are you talking about yesterday?

00:07:42.348 --> 00:07:44.455
It's finished."

00:07:45.213 --> 00:07:53.268
So, with this kind of idea that somebody has
harmed us, somebody is horrid to us we linger on

00:07:54.627 --> 00:07:56.654
in the past.

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.485
So, the wisdom of Sahaja Yoga is in understanding

00:08:02.566 --> 00:08:07.565
the limitations up to which you can go to express your anger,

00:08:07.679 --> 00:08:14.604
to express your revenge, so called,

00:08:14.817 --> 00:08:17.700
on anyone whatsoever.

00:08:19.849 --> 00:08:25.432
But the best thing would be to leave it to the Divine power,

00:08:25.513 --> 00:08:29.488
because everything is done by Divine power.

00:08:29.575 --> 00:08:33.339
We all exist inside the Divine power.